WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:07.620
Yes time to lose a few more loved ones&nbsp;
as today we are diving back into Jujutsu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:14.340
Kaisens culling game and let me just say,&nbsp;
This isn't just any old colony aswell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:20.940
we are FINALLY back with the gambling&nbsp;
mad man himself Hakari in Tokyo Colony 2.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:41.760
So to start things off here we are actually&nbsp;
throwing away any idea of that culling game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.200
and going back to before the country wide idle&nbsp;
transfiguration where a young man with blue hair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.640
and blue eyes named Charles Bernard filled&nbsp;
out his visitor's registration at Shueisha's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.720
publishing house in Tokyo. Two of the staff&nbsp;
members noticed and discussed if he brought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.220
in a manga submission also commenting on&nbsp;
how unusual it is for a Gaijin to do so.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:04.140
Charles later ends up meeting a Shueisha staff&nbsp;
member to review his manga submission. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:08.160
improperly sitting on a desk, Charles expressed&nbsp;
that he's always pondered what makes a manga&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.000
creator. They don't need licenses and&nbsp;
in Charles' opinion, experience doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.460
necessarily validate a creation either. (Which&nbsp;
makes sense, like Isayama for example had never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:22.020
made a manga before attack on Titan ANYYYWAYYYS)&nbsp;
The employee looked over Bernard's manga while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:28.080
hardly listening to his words, wishing he would&nbsp;
just sit in a chair. He only commented that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.380
foreigner's Japanese is pretty good but Charles&nbsp;
responded by repeating the same sentiment back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:35.400
confusing the man. (Hate cutting myself off&nbsp;
this much, BUT if you guys watch anyone who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:40.740
lives in Japanese and is a foreigner this is&nbsp;
a pretty common thing to hear to the point its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:47.820
almost an underhand insult) The employee&nbsp;
stated that's obviously the case because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:52.320
he's Japanese and Charles reveals that he was&nbsp;
born and raised in Japan although his parents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.700
are French. The employee apologized for assuming&nbsp;
and Charles dismissed it because he believed it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:59.820
would be the start of a long relationship&nbsp;
between him and the publishing studio.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:04.800
YET, This DOG of a Shueisha employee&nbsp;
is mostly unimpressed by Charles' manga&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:08.400
submission and critiques the story,&nbsp;
the genre, the tone, and most of all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:12.960
the artwork. He used one example of one panel&nbsp;
where a character's finger is bent too much in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:17.220
one direction. The employee tries to show Charles&nbsp;
by pointing his own finger in demonstration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:20.880
but Charles immediately breaks it&nbsp;
to match the manga's art. Irritated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:26.040
Charles told the man to watch movies or stare at&nbsp;
photos if he wanted realistic artwork. He believed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:30.180
a publishing house should appreciate the passion&nbsp;
that can't be replicated in precise artwork.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:34.620
Charles finishes his tirade after assaulting&nbsp;
the employee and storms out of the building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:38.760
deeming the entire experience a waste of&nbsp;
time. SO YEAH DUNNO WHAT THAT WAS ABOUT!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:43.050
probably just a small warning from Gege to&nbsp;
any future publishers about his artwork haha

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:46.800
Skipping forward now though to the fateful day&nbsp;
of November the 12th we find that somehow this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:51.540
pure manga reading degenerate Charles is outside&nbsp;
and on a ferries wheel with Kinji Hakari inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:55.260
of the culling game. He asks Hakari if he&nbsp;
knows exactly what makes someone a manga&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:59.820
creator, yet as we could probably imagine, an&nbsp;
annoyed, Hakari answers that he doesn't care.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:06.360
Just lacking, Charles is thankful there is still&nbsp;
electricity powering the area but Hakari isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:10.560
and suggests he normally wouldn't ride a Ferris&nbsp;
wheel with another man. Charles points out that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:15.360
could've refused but Hakari wants to scope out the&nbsp;
area in case he brings a girl back one day, cause&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:19.800
ya know big brain thinking n all pre planning for&nbsp;
future events as the man knows the culling game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:25.140
aint gonna merc him. Charles is surprised Hakari&nbsp;
believes Tokyo will recover from the Culling Game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:30.360
claiming that he is the exact opposite, as someone&nbsp;
who's only come to gaze upon the end of it all.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:35.100
Ever since curses flooded Tokyo, there haven't&nbsp;
been outlets for manga, and creators that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:39.660
Charles respected are giving up. Charles asks&nbsp;
Hakari to give him a reason to fight because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:43.800
the heroes in battle manga's are always fighting&nbsp;
for positive reasons while the Culling Game only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:48.600
incites fights for negative ones. Charles asks&nbsp;
Hakari to provoke him enough to instill hatred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:53.280
inside of him the point where he could take&nbsp;
him out without remorse. Hearing this, Hakari&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:58.380
decides to oblige and thoroughly insults Charles.&nbsp;
He says he would never read Charles' creepy manga&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:02.760
because his gloomy disposition might infect him.&nbsp;
Then in probably the best line of the entire damn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:07.800
manga so far, he also tells Charles to stop&nbsp;
whining and to start fighting, YOU CREEPY&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:13.260
OTAKU. INSULTED AND with tears in his eyes,&nbsp;
Charles asks why he’d say such a mean thing?

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:18.600
Ready to fight Hakari for his rude comments,&nbsp;
Charles conjures the G Warstaff, a pen-shaped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:22.860
spear. Immediately he attacks, bursting through&nbsp;
their pod and forcing Hakari outside on top of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:26.760
ferris wheel where his assault continues.&nbsp;
Charles thrusts his spear at Hakari's head&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:31.500
several times while quoting a "poem" from a&nbsp;
creator he admires. Hakari simply avoids the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:35.280
strikes and jumps off the ferris wheel onto a&nbsp;
building below, causing the Frenchman to chase&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:39.600
after. Standing there its shown that or special&nbsp;
grade demon is a lil annoyed because Charles is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:44.100
actually quoting a comment from Katsura Hoshino,&nbsp;
which Hakari just doesn't consider a poem.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:49.020
Charles expands upon the "poem" by explaining&nbsp;
that a mangaka enters a fictitious space in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:54.480
their minds where anything is possible because to&nbsp;
them reality just isn't satisfying. He continues&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:59.340
stating he believes his reality has been overtaken&nbsp;
by jujutsu and because of this he has lost his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:05.040
motivation as both a manga reader and creator. He&nbsp;
asks Hakari what that feeling is called and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:10.440
suspended student replies with that he’s getting&nbsp;
bored. As his fighting spirit begins rising,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:13.920
Charles suggests that the feeling&nbsp;
he’s got is called despair instead.

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:18.420
Fueled by sorrow for his opponent, Charles&nbsp;
strikes hard with his G Warstaff and scratches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:23.220
Hakari's cheek open, drawing a bit of blood at&nbsp;
the pen's tip. Noticing that the spear is a pen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:27.060
Hakari asks him if it's okay for a mangaka&nbsp;
to use their drawing pen for violence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:31.860
but Charles argues using a reference from&nbsp;
Captain Tsubasa. Following this he activates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:35.280
the condition for his cursed technique&nbsp;
and marks Hakari with a glowing square.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:40.320
Curiously confused Hakari asks what's going on&nbsp;
as he throws a flying kick but Charles is able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:44.820
to avoid it and immediately counterattacks with&nbsp;
an attack surprising the former. Easily though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:48.900
Hakari maintains his balance as he's knocked&nbsp;
back several meters from the blow, although he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:54.180
personally didnt take any damage, his sleeve was&nbsp;
cut open. While examining the tear, Hakari also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:58.620
analyzes the way the Frenchman moved and decides&nbsp;
that it has to be more than a simple reflex.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.980
Noticing that the Special Grade Sorcerer&nbsp;
took his hands out of his pockets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:06.060
Charles taunts him for it and then&nbsp;
explains that the glowing square is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:09.840
actually a manga panel that lets the user&nbsp;
see their opponent's next move. Currently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:14.340
the Frenchman can only see one second in advance&nbsp;
but as the pen tip fills with Hakari's blood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:18.780
the former will be able to see further into&nbsp;
the future. Having heard this, Hakari dashes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:22.500
straight at Charles to confirm this abilities&nbsp;
effect and nearly lands a powerful right hook,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:26.340
with the latter admitting it would've taken&nbsp;
him out if not for the effect of G Warstaff.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:30.720
Quickly after Charles counters his attack and&nbsp;
hits Hakari across the head with the blunt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:34.560
end of his spear, affirming to him that&nbsp;
the Frenchman really can see the future!

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:39.840
However, Hakari is unimpressed by the dudes&nbsp;
ability and disappears from Charles' line of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:43.920
sight, before he re appears and punches Charles&nbsp;
in the back, stating that he still needs to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:47.880
able to see him in order to see the future&nbsp;
through his technique. To counter, Hakari&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:52.200
attacks Charles repeatedly from his blindspots&nbsp;
without letting up. In an attempt to retaliate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:56.520
Charles tries to stab Hakari in the back but the&nbsp;
latter has already anticipated he would try that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.520 --> 00:07:00.600
and intercepts before striking him again.&nbsp;
Before Charles can turn around and recover,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:05.040
Hakari completely and utterly blitzes him while&nbsp;
stating that he can't just go easy on him because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:09.720
he knows Charles would just selfishly attack&nbsp;
someone else later. Continuing Hakari believes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:14.040
that in to stop this he needs to utterly break&nbsp;
Charles and hits him with an extremely powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:18.060
punch. Then he quickly goes to get behind him&nbsp;
again, but Charles is able to recover from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:22.200
previous punch in time and reactively strikes his&nbsp;
blindspot, slightly cutting Hakari's forehead.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:27.240
Irate over how the battles going, Charles claims&nbsp;
that the vessel containing his heart is broken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:32.340
and is now spilling out in a gush of emotion. He&nbsp;
adds that now due to gaining more ink in his pen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:37.980
he can see two seconds into Hakari's future and&nbsp;
will be waiting in his blind spot. Confused as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:42.180
to why Hakari isn't intimidated, Charles&nbsp;
asks his opponent why he's just standing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:47.220
there posing while in this situation. I don't&nbsp;
think Charles has bumped into anyone who can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:51.180
create a domain expansion and due to this&nbsp;
while Hakari stands there he uses both his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:56.520
hands to form the proper hand sign to cast&nbsp;
his domain expansion, Idle Death Gamble. Due&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.520 --> 00:08:00.480
to his domain's guaranteed effect, its rules&nbsp;
are instantly transmitted to Charles' brain.

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:07.020
(ronin) Instantly the Frenchy begins to understand&nbsp;
the rules of Hakari’s Domain Expansion. It shown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:13.200
that ‘idle death gamble’ is based on a Japanese&nbsp;
pachinko machine inspired by the shoujo series CR&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:18.120
Private Pure Love Train. During the domains active&nbsp;
phase, the user must hit the jackpot by getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:23.160
three of the same symbol, which will allow them to&nbsp;
get a bonus. There's a flow of 3 different levels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:27.000
that determines the percentage of increased&nbsp;
probability and also the probability of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:31.560
jackpot through a visual effect, which Hakari can&nbsp;
choose, though ultimately this all depends on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:36.840
so called luck Hakari refers to. Also certain&nbsp;
riichi scenarios can be activated at points&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:41.100
throughout this process, and chance boosters&nbsp;
allow for increase in the chance of a jackpot.

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:44.880
Having heard all this Charles yells out&nbsp;
annoyed by the sudden info dump that was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:49.680
literally just implanted in his brain, as the&nbsp;
first stage of Hakari’s domain begins. Quickly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:53.580
Kinji releases a green and red visual effect&nbsp;
attack, which Charles dodges out of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:57.480
way causing it to activate into a riichi&nbsp;
scenario, changing the scene around them.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:00.060
(ronin) Its explained to the&nbsp;
confused Charles that if the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:04.200
character "Yuki" passes through the gate,&nbsp;
then Hakari immediately hits the jackpot.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:07.740
Charles attempts to swipe at it, but it's&nbsp;
just a visualization so nothing happens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:11.820
meaning all he can do is wait to see&nbsp;
the result. (Whiich is kinda sus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:16.680
its almost just a guaranteed jackpot whenever&nbsp;
a Riichi scenario pops up, I wonder if thats a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:20.280
house rule type thing, referring back to how&nbsp;
his domain is based on a pachinko machine.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:25.620
(ronin) Due to the indicator being&nbsp;
weak, the riichi scenario fails&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:28.920
causing them to restart back at the&nbsp;
beginning of the Domains expansion.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:42.240
Standing there, Charles thinks about how&nbsp;
he can't use his manga cursed technique to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:46.380
predict the outcome, meaning that the process&nbsp;
will repeat continuously until he defeats him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:49.920
or Kinji draws a winner, which he&nbsp;
knows would result in his loss for him.

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:54.420
However, to Kinji's surprise, what Charles&nbsp;
is most infuriated at is the presentation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:58.500
taking the beloved Private Pure Love Train&nbsp;
manga and turning it into something bizarre&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:02.640
for gambling. He continues to try and attack,&nbsp;
questioning how long he will keep this up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:07.980
with the jackpot rate being only a 1/239,&nbsp;
however Kinji is still able to effortlessly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:12.120
dodge each attack, while confidently&nbsp;
stating he's never gone past 30 times.

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:16.560
This time Hakari activates a riichi&nbsp;
scenario with an 80% success rate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:20.640
anxiously watching the outcome while the&nbsp;
two continue to duke it out. He's unable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:25.200
to focus on Kinji's future attacks as he tries&nbsp;
to pay attention to the riichi, calling on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:30.120
"Yume" character to get on the train, in hopes&nbsp;
of preventing the jackpot. Sadly for him though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:34.320
the train leaves, and "Yume" disappears,&nbsp;
allowing Charles to slice at Hakari’s side.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:38.760
Charles explains while confidently standing there,&nbsp;
that if it was a game of skill rather than luck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:44.040
Hakari might have won, but as he turns around&nbsp;
he is shocked to find "Yume" is still standing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:49.020
there saying she missed the train, meaning&nbsp;
he had indeed actually won the jackpot.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:54.577
Quickly he darts in and kicks Charles away,&nbsp;
declaring he uses skill to grab ahold of luck.

00:10:54.577 --> 00:10:59.820
(no-operator as Panda) Elsewhere in the Tokyo&nbsp;
No. 2 Colony, Panda sits alone atop a shipping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:05.400
container in a shipyard. Upon smelling the air,&nbsp;
he notes tell that roughly three people have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:11.820
dismembered nearby. He also can hardly sense the&nbsp;
perpetrator's presence, which might suggest that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:16.260
they can freely activate their curse energy.&nbsp;
Sitting there, Panda reviews the plan that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:18.900
and everyone had agreed on beforehand, which was&nbsp;
to find and negotiate with Hana Kurusu. They’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:22.500
planned to leave the fighting to&nbsp;
Hakari, but the barrier just like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:26.760
over in Tokyo Colony No.1 with Yuji&nbsp;
and Megumi split them up upon entry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:28.975
to one of those random spawn locations.&nbsp;
Although Panda knows he must leave the area,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.975 --> 00:11:31.320
he notes that acting rashly will expose him to&nbsp;
the wrong person. After a bit more thinking, Panda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:36.517
decides to take off and rolls his cute behind off&nbsp;
the shipping container to go in search of Hana.

00:11:36.517 --> 00:11:41.280
(no-operator as Panda) Once he landed, he looks&nbsp;
both ways and sighs a breath of relief. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:47.100
at that exact moment, Hajime Kashimo walks right&nbsp;
around the corner. In a split second reaction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:50.400
Panda "plays a real life panda" by standing&nbsp;
on all fours to avert suspicion, and initially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:51.180
this works, with Hajime confusedly thinking that&nbsp;
a panda must've wandered out of the nearby Zoo.

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:56.700
However, Hajime has a omega sized brain&nbsp;
and summons his Kogane to asks if that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.700 --> 00:12:01.020
panda was a player, with the latter&nbsp;
pretty much instantly confirming it.

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:03.360
(no-operator as Panda) Witnessing this&nbsp;
happen infront of his teddy bear eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:06.540
Panda was surprised to learn&nbsp;
that they have that function.

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:10.980
Yet before Panda really even had time&nbsp;
to react, the Ancient GOD LEVEL SORCERER&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:14.580
Hajime had quickly charged at him and&nbsp;
delivered a powerful blow to his torso,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:17.460
completely erupting a large portion&nbsp;
of the stuffing holding him together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:22.560
before following up this brutal attack&nbsp;
and electrocuting him. Then not done,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:27.397
Hajime while insulting his strength hits him with&nbsp;
his staff and knocks Panda back into a container.

00:12:27.397 --> 00:12:30.360
(no-operator as Panda) Having been&nbsp;
brutally beaten, Panda notes that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:35.940
Hajime's cursed energy is similar to Megumi's&nbsp;
Nue where both have electrified cursed energy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:39.540
surging through their bodies, making it utterly&nbsp;
unblockable. With his Panda form destroyed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:42.840
the puppeteer begins transforming into his Gorilla&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:46.860
Mode and strikes Hajime with the&nbsp;
prolific Unblockable Drumming Beat.

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:51.720
Noticing a change, Hajime takes a defensive&nbsp;
stance and endures the multitude of blows. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:55.860
says that the attack wasn't too bad, but it&nbsp;
was great either and follows up by using his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.860 --> 00:13:00.180
staff to tear off Panda's right arm. Then&nbsp;
continuing with his old-school brutality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:04.140
he throws Panda's own arm straight back&nbsp;
into his face, completely blinding the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:08.880
defenseless bear allowing the Sneaky sorcerer to&nbsp;
approach from the puppets right. Darting in he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:13.260
delivers a flurry of absolutely brutal hits&nbsp;
